# `lab/records/` — Human-created executed bench records

This directory is present only when repository bench-record mode is selected.
It is the canonical repository home for what actually happened at the bench.

Use one dated, stable record per execution. Record human-supplied facts such as
protocol/version, operator, timestamps, reagent lots, sample IDs, deviations,
observations, and links to resulting `metadata/`/`data/raw/` identities. Do not
embed raw data payloads here.

Records are human-owned and durable. Agents may format or cross-check supplied
facts but may never invent, infer, or silently repair them. A missing field must
remain explicit. Read [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) and the root
[`README.md`](../../README.md) contract before editing.
